@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Gym Owner Manager
+
+Owner-only gym management app. Java 17, Spring Boot 3, REST API, JPA/SQL, with a modern web UI served from the same project.
+
+## Run in IntelliJ
+1. **File > Open** and select the `pom.xml` (open as project). Let Maven download dependencies (internet needed the first time).
+2. Make sure the Project SDK is JDK 17 or newer (File > Project Structure).
+3. Run `GymApplication.java` (green play button).
+4. Open **http://localhost:8080** and sign in with **admin / admin123** (change it in Settings > Change password).
+
+The database is an H2 file in `./data` (created automatically, nothing to install). Data survives restarts.
+H2 console: http://localhost:8080/h2-console, JDBC URL `jdbc:h2:file:./data/gymdb`, user `sa`, empty password.
+To use MySQL, edit `application.properties` (instructions are in the file).
+
+## What is included
+| Area | Features |
+|---|---|
+| Owner login | Token login, change password |
+| Dashboard | Total / active / expired members, today's check-ins, monthly revenue, expenses, profit, pending dues, 6-month chart, plan popularity, expiring soon |
+| Members | Add, edit, delete, search, filter by status and plan, photo from webcam/phone camera or upload, emergency contact, ID proof, health notes, duplicate phone check |
+| Plans | Monthly / quarterly / half-yearly / yearly (editable), price, discount %, offer note |
+| Registration | Auto expiry date, amount paid, balance due, then **PDF confirmation** (logo, Member ID, photo, plan, dates, payment, terms, signature line, QR) |
+| Payments | Cash / UPI / card, pending dues, collect due, receipts (same PDF layout), payment history |
+| Renewals | Expiring list (7/15/30 days), one-click renewal, status updates automatically |
+| Reminders | WhatsApp click-to-chat with the message pre-filled (expiry, dues); email via your mail app |
+| Expenses | Rent, electricity, salaries, equipment, etc. giving profit or loss on the dashboard |
+| Export | Members, payments, expenses as CSV (opens in Excel) |
+| Billing number | Printed on all PDFs. **Changing it requires an OTP** (see below) |
+
+## Billing number OTP
+Settings > Billing number > Change. The server generates a 6-digit OTP (valid 5 minutes, 3 attempts, 30 s resend gap) and sends it to the owner phone (`app.owner.phone`).
+In development the OTP is printed in the IntelliJ console and shown on screen (`app.otp.dev-mode=true`).
+For real SMS, implement `SmsGateway` (MSG91, Twilio, Fast2SMS...) and set `app.otp.dev-mode=false`.
+Set your real number in `application.properties` **before first run** (`app.owner.phone`).
+
+## Sending the PDF
+After registering or renewing, choose Open PDF, Share on WhatsApp or Email. Browsers can't attach files to WhatsApp/mail automatically,
+so the PDF is downloaded and the chat/mail opens with the message ready; attach the file. (The WhatsApp Business API can automate this later.)
+Re-generate any time from a member's Profile > Membership PDF.
+
+## Project layout
+```
+src/main/java/com/gymowner
+  config/      login interceptor, token store, error handling, seed data
+  model/       JPA entities (Member, Plan, Payment, Expense, Attendance, Owner, Setting)
+  repo/        Spring Data repositories
+  service/     MemberService, DashboardService, PdfService, SettingService (OTP), SmsGateway
+  controller/  REST controllers under /api
+src/main/resources/static   index.html, css/app.css, js/app.js (the UI)
+```
+
+## Main API endpoints (all except login need `Authorization: Bearer <token>`)
+`POST /api/auth/login` | `GET /api/dashboard` | `GET/POST/PUT/DELETE /api/plans`
+`GET /api/members?q=&status=&planId=` | `POST /api/members` | `PUT/DELETE /api/members/{id}` | `POST /api/members/{id}/photo`
+`GET /api/members/{id}/pdf` | `POST /api/members/{id}/renew` | `POST /api/members/{id}/pay-due` | `GET /api/members/expiring?days=7`
+`GET /api/payments` | `GET /api/payments/{id}/pdf` | `GET/POST/DELETE /api/expenses` | `POST /api/attendance/checkin`
+`GET/PUT /api/settings` | `POST /api/settings/billing-number/request-otp` | `POST /api/settings/billing-number/change`
+`GET /api/export/{members|payments|expenses}.csv`
+
+## Before going live / next steps
+- Replace the in-memory `TokenStore` with Spring Security + JWT, restrict CORS in `WebConfig`, disable the H2 console, use HTTPS (camera capture needs HTTPS off localhost).
+- Razorpay / UPI online payments: add a `PaymentGatewayService` and a webhook controller that calls `MemberService.renew/payDue`.
+- Automatic reminders: a `@Scheduled` job over `MemberService.expiring()` plus a WhatsApp/SMS provider.
+- Web/app conversion: the REST API is already separate from the UI, so a React, Angular or Flutter front end can call it directly.
